@plantuml
@startuml Facebook Connection Flow
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shading false
actor User
participant Frontend
participant BackendController
participant FacebookService
participant FacebookGateway
database Database

User -> Frontend: Click "Connect Facebook Page"
Frontend -> BackendController: GET /api/social/facebook/url?brandId={brandId}
BackendController -> FacebookService: getAuthUrl(brandId, redirectUri)
FacebookService --> BackendController: authUrl
BackendController --> Frontend: JSON { url }
Frontend -> User: Redirect to Facebook OAuth page

User -> Facebook: Login & Approve Permissions
Facebook -> BackendController: GET /api/social/facebook/callback?code={code}&state={brandId}
BackendController -> FacebookService: connectChannel(brandId, code, redirectUri)
FacebookService -> FacebookGateway: exchangeCodeForToken(code, redirectUri)
FacebookGateway --> FacebookService: User Access Token
FacebookService -> FacebookGateway: getUserPages(userAccessToken)
FacebookGateway --> FacebookService: List of Pages (id, name, access_token, category, etc.)
note over FacebookService: Select first page or default for connection\n(Or use a Page Selector if UI permits)
FacebookService -> FacebookGateway: getPageDetails(pageId, pageAccessToken)
FacebookGateway --> FacebookService: Page stats (likes, followers, about, name, picture)
FacebookService -> FacebookGateway: getPageAnalytics(pageId, pageAccessToken, startDate, endDate)
FacebookGateway --> FacebookService: Clicks, Impressions, Growth, Demographics
FacebookService -> Database: upsertFacebookAccount(brandId, pageData, pageAccessToken, analytics)
Database --> FacebookService: Saved Account & Analytics
FacebookService --> BackendController: Success
BackendController -> Frontend: Redirect /manage/connections?success=facebook_connected
@enduml
